<p>Most people who wear glasses every day have never actually shopped for eyewear. They&#8217;ve bought whatever a big-box retailer had in stock that fit their insurance benefit. That&#8217;s a different experience from what happens at a boutique that curates its own collection, and it&#8217;s worth understanding why before you spend real money on your next pair.</p>
<p>At Austin Optics in Forest Hills, the eyewear wall is personally chosen by <a href="{{ route('meet-the-team') }}">Iris</a>, a licensed optician with more than 30 years in the industry, including time at a Park Avenue boutique and a long run at a Brooklyn Heights practice before she returned to Queens. She carries Silhouette, Face à Face, Chopard, Anne et Valentin, and Lafont, and she&#8217;ll tell you flat out that she&#8217;s turned away plenty of other brands to keep that list short.</p>
